    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193-a1">

                <pb facs="0278" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg170"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    195.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Bravo to Mr. Shannon.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry for
                            Foreign Affairs</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName><placeName type="venue"><hi rendition="#italic">National
                                    Palace</hi></placeName>
                            <placeName type="city"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Managua</hi></placeName></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic">September 14,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: For the information of your
                    excellency’s Government I take the liberty of herewith inclosing a copy of the
                    note addressed by this ministry, yesterday, to his excellency Charles Audley
                    Gosling, Her Britannic Majesty’s minister plenipotentiary in Central America,
                    regarding the state of affairs in the Mosquito Reservation.</p>
                <p>I renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jorge Bravo.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
